      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the man in <Picture 1>, with layered shoulder-length blonde hair, a knowing smirk, a black satin long-sleeve shirt with a deep V-neck, three layered necklaces including a lion-head pendant, black dress trousers, a black belt with a silver buckle, and black leather dress shoes.\n<Subject 2> is the woman in <Picture 2>, with jet-black hair in a high bun with side-swept bangs and a pearl-and-silver hair ornament, a floor-length black velvet off-shoulder gown, a four-strand pearl choker, pearl drop earrings, multi-strand pearl bracelets on both wrists, deep red lipstick, and black pointed heels.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video shows <Subject 1> and <Subject 2> dancing the first dance at a wedding where the guests take him for the groom; she knows the real groom is already dead. Two reference images define the pair; the ballroom is generated from the written scene.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4]): fully_preserved - blonde wolf-cut, black satin deep-V, layered necklaces, lion-head pendant, black trousers, and dress shoes are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4]): fully_preserved - high bun, pearl hair ornament, black velvet off-shoulder gown, pearl choker, drop earrings, bracelets, red lipstick, and black heels are retained.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is live-action, photorealistic, set in a hotel ballroom at night. Warm chandelier light, gold wall panels, a pale dance floor, out-of-focus guests in dark formalwear forming a ring. No one else is identified as a subject.\n[Shot 1] A wide two-shot, diagonal composition, locked near-static (about 10% movement). <Subject 1> and <Subject 2> stand at the center of the floor in closed dance hold. He is the man from <Picture 1>, left hand at her waist, the lion-head pendant resting on the open V of the black satin shirt, blonde hair catching chandelier light, the familiar smirk already on. She is the woman from <Picture 2>, right hand on his shoulder, black velvet gown spreading on the floor, pearl choker tight at the throat, bun unmoving. Guests watch. They begin a slow turn.\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the camera cuts to an over-the-shoulder close-up from behind <Subject 1> onto <Subject 2>'s face. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed (about 25%). Her red mouth barely moves. <Subject 2> (S1) says in a low, even, private voice meant only for him: <d>[Chinese] 别笑得那么像他。</d> Her eyes stay on his mouth, not on the guests.\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.000, the camera cuts to a reverse close-up of <Subject 1> (S2), 180°, chandelier catchlights in his amber-brown eyes. The smirk does not drop. He answers, lazy, amused, close to her ear: <d>[Chinese] 合同没写不能笑。</d> They keep turning. The lion pendant shifts once against the satin.\n[Shot 4] At 00:11.000, the camera cuts to a medium two-shot at their feet and then tilts up. On the second turn <Subject 2> plants her black heel on the toe of his dress shoe — not a stumble, a press — and holds it for a beat. His smirk flickers. The camera orbits with small amplitude at slow speed (about 30%) around them and settles on their faces still in hold. Velvet and satin stay identical to <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>. Guests remain soft rings of bokeh.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA low ballroom murmur and glass clinks sit under a distant string quartet that is diegetic in the room. Shoe leather turns on the floor. Her heel presses his toe with a short, hard tap. Fabric of velvet and satin rubs once per turn.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A\n"
